<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf8">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="./spec.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/highlight.js/8.4/styles/github.min.css">
<script src="./spec.js"></script>
<pre class="metadata">
title: TypedArray.prototype.search / searchLast / contains
stage: 1
contributors: James M Snell
</pre>

<emu-clause id="sec-typedarray-objects">
  <h1>TypedArray Objects</h1>

  <emu-clause id="sec-%typedarray%-intrinsic-object">
    <h1>The %TypedArray% Intrinsic Object</h1>

    <emu-clause id="sec-abstract-operations-for-typedarray-objects">
      <h1>Abstract Operations for TypedArray Objects</h1>

      <emu-clause id="sec-typedarraysearchsubsequence" type="abstract operation">
        <h1>
          TypedArraySearchSubsequence (
            _O_: a TypedArray,
            _needle_: a TypedArray,
            _direction_: ~first~ or ~last~,
          ): either a normal completion containing an integral Number or a throw completion
        </h1>
        <dl class="header">
          <dt>description</dt>
          <dd>It searches for an occurrence of the subsequence _needle_ within _O_, returning the index of the match or *-1*<sub>𝔽</sub> if not found. The _direction_ parameter controls whether the first or last match is returned.</dd>
        </dl>
        <emu-alg>
          1. Let _taRecord_ be ? ValidateTypedArray(_O_, ~seq-cst~).
          1. Let _needleRecord_ be ? ValidateTypedArray(_needle_, ~seq-cst~).
          1. If TypedArrayElementType(_O_) is not TypedArrayElementType(_needle_), throw a *TypeError* exception.
          1. Let _haystackLength_ be TypedArrayLength(_taRecord_).
          1. Let _needleLength_ be TypedArrayLength(_needleRecord_).
          1. If _needleLength_ is 0, then
            1. If _direction_ is ~first~, return *+0*<sub>𝔽</sub>.
            1. Else, return 𝔽(_haystackLength_).
          1. If _needleLength_ &gt; _haystackLength_, return *-1*<sub>𝔽</sub>.
          1. <emu-meta effects="user-code">If _direction_ is ~first~, let _index_ be the smallest non-negative integer _k_ such that the subsequence of _O_ starting at _k_ with length _needleLength_ is SameValueZero-equal to _needle_, or *-1*<sub>𝔽</sub> if no such _k_ exists.</emu-meta>
          1. Else, let _index_ be the largest non-negative integer _k_ such that _k_ + _needleLength_ ≤ _haystackLength_ and the subsequence of _O_ starting at _k_ with length _needleLength_ is SameValueZero-equal to _needle_, or *-1*<sub>𝔽</sub> if no such _k_ exists.
          1. Return _index_.
        </emu-alg>
        <emu-note type="editor">
          <p>The description of the subsequence search in steps 8-9 is intentionally high-level, allowing implementations freedom in how the search is performed. A question for committee is whether these steps need to be specified more precisely with explicit algorithmic substeps (e.g., element-by-element comparison with specific iteration order), even if implementations are expected to use optimized approaches such as Boyer-Moore or other string matching algorithms.</p>
        </emu-note>
        <emu-note>
          <p>This abstract operation requires that _needle_ be a TypedArray of the same type as _O_. For example, if _O_ is a `Uint8Array`, then _needle_ must also be a `Uint8Array`.</p>
          <p>Two subsequences are <dfn>SameValueZero-equal</dfn> if they have the same length and for each index, the corresponding elements are equal according to the SameValueZero algorithm. This means that for floating-point TypedArrays (Float32Array, Float64Array, Float16Array), *NaN* values are considered equal to each other regardless of their bit patterns, and *+0*<sub>𝔽</sub> is considered equal to *-0*<sub>𝔽</sub>.</p>
          <p>Implementations may use any technique to search for the subsequence, such as naive search, Boyer-Moore, or other string matching algorithms, provided the observable result is correct.</p>
        </emu-note>
      </emu-clause>
    </emu-clause>

    <emu-clause id="sec-properties-of-the-%typedarrayprototype%-object">
      <h1>Properties of the %TypedArray% Prototype Object</h1>

      <emu-clause id="sec-%typedarray%.prototype.search">
        <h1>%TypedArray%.prototype.search ( _needle_ )</h1>
        <p>This method searches for the first occurrence of the subsequence _needle_ within this TypedArray. It performs the following steps when called:</p>
        <emu-alg>
          1. Let _O_ be the *this* value.
          1. Return ? TypedArraySearchSubsequence(_O_, _needle_, ~first~).
        </emu-alg>
      </emu-clause>

      <emu-clause id="sec-%typedarray%.prototype.searchlast">
        <h1>%TypedArray%.prototype.searchLast ( _needle_ )</h1>
        <p>This method searches for the last occurrence of the subsequence _needle_ within this TypedArray. It performs the following steps when called:</p>
        <emu-alg>
          1. Let _O_ be the *this* value.
          1. Return ? TypedArraySearchSubsequence(_O_, _needle_, ~last~).
        </emu-alg>
      </emu-clause>

      <emu-clause id="sec-%typedarray%.prototype.contains">
        <h1>%TypedArray%.prototype.contains ( _needle_ )</h1>
        <p>This method determines whether the subsequence _needle_ exists within this TypedArray. It performs the following steps when called:</p>
        <emu-alg>
          1. Let _O_ be the *this* value.
          1. Let _index_ be ? TypedArraySearchSubsequence(_O_, _needle_, ~first~).
          1. If _index_ is *-1*<sub>𝔽</sub>, return *false*.
          1. Return *true*.
        </emu-alg>
      </emu-clause>
    </emu-clause>
  </emu-clause>
</emu-clause>
